  "body": "Found while working #835 (PR stacked on #837).\n\n**What happens.** #835 moves the verdict laws that read the tool's stack above the shank - reach (c), the mid-turn sweep (c3), the solid law (b2), the containment solid law, posed rapids and the rotary field law - onto the body's band stack (`Cutter::body`, `tool_body::stack`), the shape the simulation draws. Three laws still read one holder cylinder by construction and so judge a modelled tool body (#368 mesh, #93 drawn profile) by the cylinder enclosing it:\n\n- `crates/app/src/operation/drill_reach.rs` - the axial holder-face law and `cross_holder` (one disc / tube at `holder_d`, from the shank top);\n- `crates/app/src/operation/cross_part.rs` - `part_clear` builds `Cutter::of(tool)` without the body;\n- `crates/app/src/operation/probe_op.rs` - `stylus_cutter` folds stem and holder into one band.\n\nThey over-report only (never smaller than the body), and since #835 their refusals / the probe path say so by name (\"the tool body is judged here by the cylinder enclosing it, Ø...\"). But a stepped body (narrow nose under a wide flange) can still be refused for a flange that never reaches the stock.\n\n**Expected.** Each reads the band stack: drill reach checks each band's face disc against the material over that band's radius; cross_part takes the body-carrying cutter; the stylus is rebuilt as stem + the body's bands.\n\nEvidence: `docs/decisions/835-reach-reads-band-stack.md` (kept-cylinder list), `operation::body_judged`.\n\nDone means: those three laws read the same band stack the simulation draws, with a pinning test per law for a stepped body whose nose clears and whose flange does not reach, and the enclosure wording is dropped from them.\n\nPart of #743.\n",
